From: Higor Prado <higorevop@gmail.com> (original author)
Backport-of: https://github.com/Alexays/Waybar/pull/5013
Subject: [PATCH] fix(hyprland/workspaces): adapt dispatch commands for Lua IPC protocol

Hyprland 0.54 replaced the text-based dispatch socket protocol with a
Lua-based one. Commands like "dispatch workspace 1" are now interpreted
as invalid Lua (return hl.dispatch(workspace 1)), breaking workspace
clicks in Waybar's hyprland/workspaces module on Hyprland >= 0.54.

This patch backports the upstream fix from PR #5013 (commit e17c0d9f0)
to Waybar 0.15.0:

* Adds IPC::dispatch() that probes the running Hyprland on first call
  and routes commands through the new hl.dsp Lua API when the Lua
  protocol is detected, falling back to the old text format otherwise.
* Adds IPC::buildLuaDispatch() to map old-style dispatchers to the new
  Lua hl.dsp API.
* Updates Workspace::handleClicked in workspace.cpp to use IPC::dispatch
  for all four dispatchers (workspace, focusworkspaceoncurrentmonitor,
  togglespecialworkspace with and without arg).

The upstream patch also updates Workspaces::handleScroll for scroll-
workspace-switch; that code path does not exist in 0.15.0 (the
all-outputs / scroll-up / scroll-down workspace switching was added
on master after 0.15.0) so this backport skips it.

Drop this patch once waybar 0.15.x is bumped to a release that includes
the upstream fix (likely 0.15.1 or later, or whatever ships first).

diff --git a/include/modules/hyprland/backend.hpp b/include/modules/hyprland/backend.hpp
index 2e0ef65..60ef088 100644
--- a/include/modules/hyprland/backend.hpp
+++ b/include/modules/hyprland/backend.hpp
@@ -19,6 +19,19 @@ class EventHandler {
 
 /// If you want to use the Hyprland IPC, simply use IPC::inst() to get the singleton instance.
 /// Do not create multiple instances.
+  /// Dispatch a Hyprland command. Automatically uses the correct protocol
+  /// (legacy text or Lua-based) depending on the running Hyprland version.
+  static std::string dispatch(const std::string& dispatcher, const std::string& arg);
+
+  /// Build a Lua-format dispatch command string.
+  static std::string buildLuaDispatch(const std::string& dispatcher, const std::string& arg);
+
+  /// Detect whether the running Hyprland uses the Lua-based IPC protocol.
+  /// Returns true for Hyprland >= 0.54 (Lua config), false for older versions.
+  static bool isLuaProtocol();
+
+  static std::optional<bool> s_luaProtocolDetected_;  // cached detection result
+
 class IPC {
  protected:
   IPC();  // use IPC::inst() instead.
